Claude Desktop / Cursor / WindsurfClaude CodeVS CodeHosted (remote HTTP)LangChain / Semantic Kernel / custom <p>Add to the client's MCP config: <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code> for Claude Desktop, <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code> (or <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> in a project) for Cursor.</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "whiteboxxai": {
      "command": "whiteboxxai-mcp",
      "env": {
        "WHITEBOXXAI_MCP_API_BASE_URL": "https://api.whiteboxxai.com",
        "WHITEBOXXAI_MCP_API_KEY": "wbx_live_..."
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>claude mcp add whiteboxxai \
  --env WHITEBOXXAI_MCP_API_KEY=wbx_live_... \
  -- whiteboxxai-mcp
</code></pre> <p>Or add the same <code>mcpServers</code> block as Claude Desktop to a project's <code>.mcp.json</code>. Don't commit a real key; reference an environment variable such as <code>${WHITEBOXXAI_MCP_API_KEY}</code> in the file.</p> <p>VS Code uses a <code>servers</code> key in <code>.vscode/mcp.json</code>, and can prompt for the key instead of storing it:</p> <pre><code>{
  "inputs": [
    {
      "type": "promptString",
      "id": "whitebox-key",
      "description": "WhiteBoxXAI API key",
      "password": true
    }
  ],
  "servers": {
    "whiteboxxai": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "whiteboxxai-mcp",
      "env": {
        "WHITEBOXXAI_MCP_API_KEY": "${input:whitebox-key}"
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>For clients that support remote MCP servers. With Claude Code:</p> <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http whiteboxxai https://api.whiteboxxai.com/mcp/ \
  --header "Authorization: Bearer wbx_live_..."
</code></pre> <p>In a JSON config that supports remote servers:</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "whiteboxxai": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://api.whiteboxxai.com/mcp/",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer wbx_live_..." }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>Any MCP client library can start <code>whiteboxxai-mcp</code> over stdio with the environment above, or connect to the hosted endpoint with an <code>Authorization</code> header. For LangChain, the <code>langchain-mcp-adapters</code> package loads the tools into an agent.</p> <p>More copy-paste definitions are on Agent Config Definitions.</p>
